.TH CHTTPSVR_REQ_HEADER 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttpsvr_req_header \- look up a request header
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <chttpserver.h>

const char *chttpsvr_req_header(const chttpsvr_req *req,
                                 const char *name);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Returns the value of the request header named name, or NULL if the
header is absent.  The lookup is case-insensitive.  When a header
appears multiple times, the last value is returned.

The returned pointer is valid for the lifetime of the handler
invocation.
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
A chunked request body's trailer fields (RFC 7230 4.1.2) are indexed
exactly like any other header and become retrievable through this same
function once they have actually been parsed; there is no separate
trailer-specific accessor.

For a buffered route this is transparent: the handler only ever runs
once the whole body, trailers included, has already been read, so a
trailer field is retrievable from the very start of the handler.

For a streaming route, a trailer field becomes retrievable only once
the handler's own chttpsvr_req_read() calls have drained the body all
the way to its natural end (a return of 0).  Querying it any earlier
returns NULL, indistinguishable from the field never having been sent
at all.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpsvr_req_method (3),
.BR chttpsvr_req_path (3),
.BR chttpsvr_req_read (3)
